        </div>
      </div>
      
      <div class="faq-item" role="region">
        <button class="faq-item__question" aria-expanded="false">
          What denier is best for a turnout rug?
          <span class="faq-item__icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
        </button>
        <div class="faq-item__answer" hidden>
          <p>600D suits horses turned out alone or with a calm companion and is the most economical option. 1200D is the most common middle ground, offering noticeably better tear resistance for a moderate cost increase. 1680D is the toughest option, suited to horses turned out in groups or known to be hard on rugs, at a higher price point.</p>
